<article class="env-lemma" id="0GDA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GDA">Lemma <span data-tag="0GDA">88.22.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of formal algebraic spaces. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ and $Y$ are locally Noetherian, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\Delta _ f : X \to X \times _ Y X$ is rig-étale and rig-surjective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $f$ is rig surjective if and only if every adic morphism $\text{Spf}(R) \to Y$ where $R$ is a complete discrete valuation ring lifts to a morphism $\text{Spf}(R) \to X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      One direction is trivial. For the other, suppose that $\text{Spf}(R) \to Y$ is an adic morphism such that there exists an extension of complete discrete valuation rings $R \subset R'$ with $\text{Spf}(R') \to \text{Spf}(R) \to X$ factoring through $Y$. Consider the fibre product diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \text{Spf}(R') \ar[r] \ar[rd] &  \text{Spf}(R) \times _ Y X \ar[r] \ar[d]^ p &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  &  \text{Spf}(R) \ar[r] &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The morphism $p$ is locally of finite type as a base change of $f$, see Formal Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AQ5" data-tag="0AQ5">87.24.4</a>. The diagonal morphism $\Delta _ p$ is the base change of $\Delta _ f$ and hence is rig-étale and rig-surjective. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0GD9" data-tag="0GD9">88.22.2</a> the flat locus of $\text{Spf}(R) \times _ Y X$ over $R$ is either $\emptyset $ or equal to $\text{Spf}(R)$. However, since $\text{Spf}(R')$ factors through it we conclude it is not empty and hence we get a morphism $\text{Spf}(R) \to \text{Spf}(R) \times _ Y X \to X$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>